{"class":"fixable","chokepoint":[{"operator":"async I/O page reads of orders_cust","component":"asynchronous I/O layer","frozen":true,"why_every_version_executes_it":"count(DISTINCT cust) must read the cust values. The smallest structure holding them is the orders_cust index, and every page read passes through the frozen I/O layer.","least_work":{"amount":730,"unit":"pages","per_unit_cost_us":1.0,"total_ms":0.73,"calling_context":"one sequential scan of the covering index, warm OS page cache, each page read once"}}],"floor_ms":0.73,"L_delta":-1.68,"rationale":"Turso spends its time in hashing for distinct: SipHash, hash_one and op_hash_distinct inside the VDBE, which is mutable. The orders_cust scan already delivers cust in sorted order, so the planner/VDBE can count distinct values by comparing each to the previous one, as SQLite does. Start-up overhead is also mutable. The frozen I/O work is about 0.73 ms, well below 3.9 ms, so no architectural floor exists."}
